    '53': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'trima', code: '53', name: 'DISCONNECT TEST ALERT', statusLine: 'Donor disconnect error', messageType: 'R1 file:///C:/Users/cmararb/AppData/Local/Temp/~hhFFBB.htm 9/26/2026 7.0 Alarms Page 54 of 292', dlogText: 'Disconnect alert', category: '', alarmId: '', occursDuring: 'Donor Disconnect', detection: 'Condition: The APS pressure is logged immediately after the operator confirms the donor is disconnected while the inlet pump is at 50mL/min until the APS pressure reaches -100 mmHg OR (if lower than -100 mmHg, 10mmHg less than logged pressure) then monitors the decay of the pressure for 6 seconds. Detection: The pressure does not reach one of the limits above after 30 seconds. After three attempts a disconnect test alarm is generated. Detection: The pressure decays too much within 6 seconds.', possibleCauses: 'l Donor line clamp is not closed. l Negative pressure in access line exceeds access low alarm limit before -100 mmHg change occurs. Vent negative pressure and try test again. l Defective APS. l Defective APS/CPS Adapter CCA. l Defective I/O Two CCA l Defective Control CCA.', suggestedActions: 'Verify functionality of APS sensor by applying a known pressure and'),
