    '1301': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1301', name: 'Hydraulic system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydHardwareFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the device commands the hydraulic pump to move to a specific position, but the number of steps traveled indicates an incorrect position.', possibleCauses: 'The hydraulic pump motor coupling is slipping. Check the hydraulic pump motor for proper operation. The pump motor is defective. Replace the hydraulic pump motor. The pump motor is not responding. Check the connections to the hydraulic pump motor. The linear guide is slipping. Check the linear guide for proper operation. The piston is stuck. Manually move the piston to determine if it is stuck.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1304': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1304', name: 'Hydraulic system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydraulicCommandFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer receives an invalid hydraulic pump command.', possibleCauses: 'The Reveos device has a software issue due to either timing or incompatible versions between the device software and STS, the protocol, or the CMC. Check the compatibility of software upgrades or downgrades. Expect this alarm until the upgrades or downgrades are complete. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card. The control computer is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the control computer for proper operation and connections. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1305': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1305', name: 'Hydraulic reset', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydResetFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when during a hydraulic reset the hydraulic pump moved an excessive number of steps without tripping a limit switch. This is detected by the number of steps traveled.', possibleCauses: 'The limit switches or the position flag are defective or were incorrectly positioned. Confirm the limit switches and the position flag are correctly set and operational. The pump motor coupling is slipping. Determine whether the coupler is slipping. The pump motor is defective. Check the hydraulic pump motor for proper operation. The linear guide is defective. Check the linear guide for proper operation. The connections between the components and the e-box are defective. Check the circuit path for all of these components and look for a poor connection. The e-box is defective. Replace the e-box.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1307': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1307', name: 'Hydraulic pressure too high', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydOverpressureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Bulk expression or post-processing to end procedure', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the hydraulic pressure sensor reading indicates the hydraulic pressure is 3.5 bar or greater.', possibleCauses: 'The frangibles are unbroken or partially broken. Confirm all of the frangibles on the buckets are fully broken. The hydraulic system has too much air. Purge air from the hydraulic system. The hydraulic pressure sensor is defective. Troubleshoot the hydraulic system for air and fluid leaks. Compare hydraulic pressure sensor readings to a calibrated gauge. Replace the sensor if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1314': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1314', name: 'Hydraulic control', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydControllerFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the hydraulic pump motor generates an over-current, over-position, or overtemp fault.', possibleCauses: 'The hydraulic system is mechanically binding. Troubleshoot the piston, linear guide, and hydraulic cylinder movement. The pump motor or the linear guide is defective. Replace the hydraulic pump motor and the linear guide. The system is hydraulically locked due to an obstruction in the hydraulic system or a defective hydraulic valve. Check the valve connections and replace the valves if they are defective. Check the log files to determine which fault is being generated, and troubleshoot the system for that fault. The connections between the hydraulic system and the e-box are defective. Reseat connections on both the hydraulic pump and the e-box. If the problem persists, replace the harness. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Check the system DC voltages.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1315': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1315', name: 'Hydraulic hardware', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydPressureSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the hydraulic pressure sensor is -1 to 4 bar, which is out of range.', possibleCauses: 'The pressure sensor is defective. Compare hydraulic pressure sensor readings to a calibrated gauge. Replace the sensor if it is defective. The connection between the hydraulic pressure sensor and the control CCA is defective. Check the circuit path for all of these components looking for a poor connection. The +24 V DC power supplied to the hydraulic pressure sensor is out of range or has a defective connection. Check system DC voltages.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1317': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1317', name: 'Hydraulic pressure problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Hydraulic', alarmId: 'HydraulicsAmbientCalibrationTimeout', occursDuring: 'Startup', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the startup hydraulic calibration took longer than 60 seconds.', possibleCauses: 'An alarm during the startup state forced a hydraulic reset to take place. The hydraulic reset did not complete before the ambient pressure calculation started. The reset takes priority and can cause the system to calibrate from a false value. Force a recalibration by rebooting the device. The hydraulic pressure or the volume of the hydraulic fluid sent to the rotor was too high when the device was powered down. Check the log files to see if ambient pressure calculation started before a hydraulic reset was completed. Check to see source of alarm and troubleshoot that alarm. The hydraulic motor coupler is slipping. Determine whether the coupler is slipping. The pump motor has failed, or the power supplied to the motor has failed. Check the hydraulic motor and verify that the supply voltage is in range. The hydraulic system is leaking, the hydraulic pressure sensor has failed, or there is a communication failure. Check the hydraulic system for leaks and for proper operation.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1401': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1401', name: 'Leak detected', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LeakDetectedAlarm', occursDuring: 'During a protocol, after the outer lid has been closed.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the leak detector senses enough debris or fluid to trigger the leak detector amplifier signal to the control system.', possibleCauses: 'Fluid or debris may have touched or passed in front of the detector. Clean the leak detector, basin, and upper centrifuge. Check for hidden fluid or debris. Perform the Dry Check protocol to see if the centrifuge and basin are properly dry. The leak detector has residue or a film on its surface. Clean the leak detector surface. The leak detector amplifier was not calibrated correctly. Calibrate the leak detector using the Leak Detector Calibration Tool instructions. The leak detector amplifier is defective or there is a loose connection. Troubleshoot the system and replace the leak detector amplifier if it is defective. The leak detector is defective or there is a loose connection. Troubleshoot the system and replace the leak detector if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1403': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1403', name: 'Outer lid system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LidCommandFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer receives an invalid lid lock command.', possibleCauses: 'The Reveos device has a software issue due to either timing or incompatible versions between the device software, STS, the protocol, or the CMC. Check the compatibility of software upgrades or downgrades. Expect this alarm until the upgrades or downgrades are complete. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card. The control computer is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the control computer for proper operation and connections. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1404': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1404', name: 'Outer lid system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LidLockMovementTimeoutAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer detects that the lid lock mechanism did not reach the commanded position by the end of the 20 second time-out.', possibleCauses: 'The lid lock stepper motor is defective or there is a loose connection. Confirm the lid lock mechanism moves properly when commanded. The optical control sensors are defective or have a loose connection. Check the optical control sensors\' connections and operation. The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the lid lock CCA test points and LEDs for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1406': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1406', name: 'Outer lid detected open', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LidStateBadWithCentrifugeEnabled', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the system detected that the lid was unlocked while the centrifuge was spinning.', possibleCauses: 'The lid is locked but a sensor reports it as unlocked. Check the connection and operation of the optical sensors. The lid lock mechanism has failed. Confirm the lid lock mechanism moves properly when commanded. The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the lid lock CCA connections, test points, and LEDs for proper operation. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1413': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1413', name: 'Fan problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'FanFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the fan CCA sends a fail signal to the control CCA.', possibleCauses: 'The main blower fan is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the main blower fan for proper operation and connections. The CMC fan or its connection is defective. Check the CMC fan for proper operation and connections. The fan CCA or its connections are defective. Check the fan CCA for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Check the e-box for proper operation and connections. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system DC voltages are within specification.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1414': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1414', name: 'Stop button pressed', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'StopSwitchAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer and safety CCA detect that the stop button was pressed.', possibleCauses: 'The stop button was pressed. Wait for the device to finish resetting to a safe state then clear the alarm and proceed. The stop button is defective or has loose connections. Check the stop button for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Check the e-box for proper operation and connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1415': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1415', name: 'Basin temperature sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'BasinTempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the basin temperature sensor is out of operating range, which is less than 1 °C or greater than 50 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The basin temperature is outside of operating range due to the operating environment, a mechanical failure, or a chiller system failure. Confirm the actual basin temperature is outside of operating range. If so, determine whether it is due to the operating environment or due to a mechanical or chilled water failure. The basin temperature sensor is defective or has loose connections. Check the basin temperature sensor for proper operation and connection. The chiller CCA or its connections are defective. Check the chiller CCA for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Check the e-box for proper operation and connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1416': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1416', name: 'Bearing temperature sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'BearingTempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the bearing temperature sensor is out of operating range, which is less than 1 °C or greater than 50 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The actual bearing temperature is outside of operating range due to the operating environment, a mechanical failure, or a chiller system failure. Confirm the actual bearing temperature is outside of operating range. If so, determine whether it is due to the operating environment or due to a mechanical or chilled water failure. The bearing temperature sensor is defective or has loose connections. Check the bearing temperature sensor for proper operation and connection. The chiller CCA or its connections are defective. Check the chiller CCA for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Check the e-box for proper operation and connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1417': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1417', name: 'Inlet temperature sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'H20TempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the chiller temperature sensor is out of operating range, which is less than 1 °C or greater than 50 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The external chilled water source is not connected, energized or at operating temperature. Confirm the external chilled water source is connected, energized, and operating at the correct temperature. The chiller temperature sensor is defective or has a loose connection. Check the chiller temperature sensor for proper operation and connection. The chiller CCA or its connections are defective. Check the chiller CCA for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Check the e-box for proper operation and connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1420': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1420', name: 'Vibration sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'VibrationSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the vibration sensor displacement value is less than 8500 or greater than 29500.', possibleCauses: 'The chiller CCA is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the chiller CCA for proper operation and connections. The vibration sensor is defective or has a loose connection. Check the vibration sensor for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Check the e-box for proper operation and connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1421': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1421', name: 'Excessive vibration', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'VibrationSensorVibrationHighAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised during the initial ramp up state if the vibration sensor detects a displacement of ± 500 counts different from the baseline. The output voltage from the vibration sensor indicates excessive vibrations.', possibleCauses: 'In a two-bucket run, the counterbalance bags are placed adjacent to each other. Confirm the operator loaded the buckets correctly, that the whole blood unit volume is appropriate, and that the counterbalance bag is in good condition. The centrifuge is out of balance due to improper loading, unbalanced buckets, or incorrect device installation. Troubleshoot the centrifuge vibration system. The balance ring bearings are stuck or the balance ring is defective. Check the balance ring for proper operation. Replace it if it is defective. One of the vibration system components is defective or has a loose connection. Troubleshoot the vibration sensor system. The vibration isolators are damaged, too soft, or too hard. Replace the vibration isolators.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1422': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1422', name: 'Bearing temperature too low', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'BearingUnderTempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the bearing temperature sensor is less than the minimum limit of 2 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The actual bearing temperature is too low because the operating environment is too cold. Check the actual bearing temperature. Replaced the sensor if it is defective. Move the device if the operating environment is too cold. The bearing temperature minimum limit is set too low for the operating environment. Confirm the bearing temperature minimum value is correct for the device\'s operating environment. The bearing temperature sensor is defective or has a loose connection. Replace the bearing temperature sensor.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1423': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1423', name: 'Inlet temperature too high', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'H20OverTempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the chiller temperature sensor exceeds the maximum limit of 19 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The external chilled water source is not at operating temperature. Confirm the chiller is at operating temperature. The maximum limit value for the external chilled water source is incorrect. Confirm the maximum value is appropriate. If it is not, reset it to the default value. The chiller temperature sensor is defective. Confirm the chiller temperature sensor is accurate.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1424': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1424', name: 'Inlet temperature too low', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'H20UnderTempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the chiller temperature sensor exceeds the minimum limit of 2 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The external chilled water source is not at operating temperature. Confirm the chiller is at operating temperature. The minimum limit is not set to a value that is correct for the external chilled water source the device is connected to. Confirm the minimum value is appropriate. If it is not, reset to the default value. Defective chiller temperature sensor. Confirm the chiller temperature sensor is accurate.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1427': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1427', name: 'Outer lid lock sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LidLockSensorDiscrepancyAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the optical control sensors and the optical safety sensor report different lock states.', possibleCauses: 'One or both of the optical control sensors are defective Check the optical control sensors for proper operation and connections. The optical safety sensor is defective. Check the optical safety sensors for proper operation and connections. The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the lid lock CCA test points and LEDs for proper operation. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1429': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1429', name: 'Outer lid sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LidSensorDiscrepancyAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the reed switch and the Hall-effect sensor report a different lid position.', possibleCauses: 'The reed switch or the Hall-effect sensor is defective or there is a loose connection. Use STS to determine which sensor is not reading correctly and troubleshoot that circuit. The lid lock plate is missing at least one magnet. Replace any missing magnets. The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the lid lock CCA test points and LEDs for proper operation. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1430': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1430', name: 'Outer lid lock power', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'LidPowerCommandMismatchAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control and safety computers issue different commands for the lid power.', possibleCauses: 'The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the lid lock system to determine which component failed and replace it if it is defective. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1432': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1432', name: 'Bearing temperature too high', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'BearingOverTempFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output value of the bearing temperature sensor exceeds the maximum limit of 49 °C.', possibleCauses: 'The actual bearing temperature is too high because the operating environment is too hot. Confirm the actual bearing temperature is too hot. If so, determine if it is due to the operating environment or if one of the components in the chiller system has failed. There is a problem with the chiller system, the centrifuge bearing, or another component that is generating excessive heat inside the device. Confirm the chiller circuit is operating properly and that the bearing isn\'t producing excess heat. The belt tension is too high. Adjust the belt tension. The bearing temperature sensor is defective. Check the bearing temperature sensor for proper operation and connection.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1433': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1433', name: 'Bucket lid latch', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'Bucket1LatchSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the bucket lid sensor reports that the lid is open when centrifuge power is on.', possibleCauses: 'The bucket lid sensor is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the bucket lid sensor for proper operation and connections. Failures may not show until the system is exposed to the g-field. There is RF interference during welding. Check the log files to see if the failure occurred during RF welding. If the problem is repeatable, it could be due to a defective bucket lid position sensor or cable. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Check the e-rotor to bucket cable connections for damaged wires or defective connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1434': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1434', name: 'Bucket lid latch', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'Bucket2LatchSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the bucket lid sensor reports that the lid is open when centrifuge power is on.', possibleCauses: 'The bucket lid sensor is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the bucket lid sensor for proper operation and connections. Failures may not show until the system is exposed to the g-field. There is RF interference during welding. Check the log files to see if the failure occurred during RF welding. If the problem is repeatable, it could be due to a defective bucket lid position sensor/cable. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Check the e-rotor to bucket cable connections for damaged wires or defective connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1435': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1435', name: 'Bucket lid latch', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'Bucket3LatchSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the bucket lid sensor reports that the lid is open when centrifuge power is on.', possibleCauses: 'The bucket lid sensor is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the bucket lid sensor for proper operation and connections. Failures may not show until the system is exposed to the g-field. There is RF interference during welding. Check the log files to see if the failure occurred during RF welding. If the problem is repeatable, it could be due to a defective bucket lid position sensor/cable. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Check the e-rotor to bucket cable connections for damaged wires or defective connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1436': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1436', name: 'Bucket lid latch', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Sensor', alarmId: 'Bucket4LatchSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the bucket lid sensor reports that the lid is open when centrifuge power is on.', possibleCauses: 'The bucket lid sensor is defective or there is a loose connection. Check the bucket lid sensor for proper operation and connections. Failures may not show until the system is exposed to the g-field. There is RF interference during welding. Check the log files to see if the failure occurred during RF welding. If the problem is repeatable, it could be due to a defective bucket lid position sensor/cable. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Check the e-rotor to bucket cable connections for damaged wires or defective connections.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1500': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1500', name: 'Problem closing valve', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Valve', alarmId: 'Bucket1PlateletValveCloseFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'When valve closes.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the platelet valve failed to close before the maximum time-out limits.', possibleCauses: 'A valve is stuck in the closed position. Loosen the valve until it operates correctly. Replicate the process under what conditions the valves became stuck to verify that the valves now operate correctly. The e-rotor is defective. The problem may not appear unless the conditions under which the alarm occurred are replicated. Determine whether the problem affects just one valve or all the valves. If the problem is only with one valve, troubleshoot the e-rotor. If the problem affects all valves, troubleshoot the components that are external to the e-rotor. The connections between the e-box and the e-rotor are defective. Check the connections between the e-rotor and the e-box. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. The slip ring is faulty. Test the slip ring in different positions to check for proper brush contact. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1501': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1501', name: 'Problem opening valve', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Valve', alarmId: 'Bucket1PlateletValveOpenFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'When valve opens.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the platelet valve failed to open before the maximum time-out limits.', possibleCauses: 'A valve is stuck in the open position. Loosen the valve until it operates correctly. Replicate the process under what conditions the valves became stuck to verify that the valves now operate correctly. The e-rotor is defective. The problem may not appear unless the conditions under which the alarm occurred are replicated. Determine whether the problem affects just one valve or all the valves. If the problem is only with one valve, troubleshoot the e-rotor. If the problem affects all valves, troubleshoot the components that are external to the e-rotor. The connections between the e-rotor and the e-box are defective. Check the connections between the e-rotor and the e-box. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. The slip ring is faulty. Test the slip ring in different positions to check for proper brush contact. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1502': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1502', name: 'Problem sealing', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Valve', alarmId: 'Bucket1PlateletValveSealingFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'During valve sealing.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the sealing time is less than 1.234 seconds.', possibleCauses: 'The component valve sealing surfaces are dirty. Clean the component valve anvils using the procedure from the operator\'s manual. The tubing is incorrect, the tubing is the incorrect temperature, or the tubing has moisture. Use only Reveos tubing that is clean, dry, and at room temperature. The tubing was misloaded under the valve anvil. Verify that the tubing is properly loaded under the component valve anvils. The RF welding circuit or connections are defective. Troubleshoot the RF welding and control circuits using the e-rotor block diagram. The connection between the RF power supply and the e-box is defective. Replace any defective connections. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Determine whether the problem affects just one valve or all the valves. If the problem is only with one valve, troubleshoot the e-rotor. If the problem affects all valves, troubleshoot the components that are external to the e-rotor. The slip ring is faulty. Test the slip ring in different positions to check for proper brush contact. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1503': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1503', name: 'Valve problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Valve', alarmId: 'Bucket1PlateletValveSoftwareFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer receives an invalid valve command.', possibleCauses: 'The Reveos device has a software issue due to either timing or incompatible versions among the device software, STS, the protocol, and the CMC. Check the compatibility of software upgrades or downgrades. Expect this alarm until the upgrades or downgrades are complete. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card. The control computer or its connections are defective. Check the control computer for proper operation and connections. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1505': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1505', name: 'Problem closing valve', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Valve', alarmId: 'Bucket2PlateletValveCloseFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'When valve closes.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the platelet valve failed to close before the maximum time-out limits.', possibleCauses: 'A valve is stuck in the closed position. If the valve is stuck unjam the valve. Refer to the e-rotor troubleshooting section. The e-rotor is defective. The problem may not appear unless the conditions under which the alarm occurred are replicated. If the problem is only with one valve, the source most likely exists within the e-rotor. Problems that affect all valves may be a failure external to the e-rotor. Refer to the e-rotor troubleshooting section. The connections between the e-box and the e-rotor are defective. Check the connections between e-rotor and e-box. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace if defective. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm system power supply voltages are in range under load. The slip ring is faulty. Test the slip ring in different positions to check for proper brush contact a full 360° of rotation. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
