    '1600': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1600', name: 'Outer lid system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Communication', alarmId: 'LidCommFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer cannot communicate with the lid lock CCA.', possibleCauses: 'Noise or failure occurred on the RS-485 communication line to the lid lock CCA. Troubleshoot what may be causing the noise or failure. The error may resolve on its own. The control computer or the RS-485 connection on the control CCA is busy and unable to communicate with other systems. This alarm will be triggered if the control CCA sends a command to the lid lock system and does not receive a response. Another system may prevent the control system from communicating. Check the log files to determine which system is at fault. Then check power and communication lines to that system. The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the lid lock CCA test points and LEDs for proper power and communication operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1601': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1601', name: 'Motor controller', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Communication', alarmId: 'MotorCommFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer cannot communicate with the centrifuge motor controller.', possibleCauses: 'Noise or failure occurred on the RS-232 communication line to the CMC. Troubleshoot what may be causing the noise or failure. The error may resolve on its own. The control computer or the RS-485 connection on the control CCA is busy and unable to communicate with other systems. This alarm will be triggered if the control CCA sends a command to the lid lock system and does not receive a response. Another system may prevent the control system from communicating. Check the log files to determine which system is at fault. Then check power and communication lines to that system. The centrifuge motor controller or its connections are defective. Check the CMC for proper power and communication operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Determine whether any of the e-rotor cables or bucket cables are pinched, smashed, or kinked. Also check them for continuity and shorts. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
