    '1800': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1800', name: 'System problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'SoftwareWatchdogFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when a control software watchdog failure occurs.', possibleCauses: 'The control computer did not receive the watchdog message back from the safety computer. Power cycle to clear the alarm. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent. The ethernet connection between the safety computer and the control computer is defective. Check the ethernet connection between the safety and control computers. The safety computer or its connections are defective. Check the safety computer for proper operation and connections. The control computer or its connections are defective. Check the control computer for proper operation and connections. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1801': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1801', name: 'System problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'SoftwareStartupFault', occursDuring: 'Startup.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer is unable to establish communication with the safety computer, lid lock CCA, or e-rotor.', possibleCauses: 'The safety computer, the lid lock CCA, or the e-rotor is defective. Check the log files to determine which system is at fault. Then check power and communication lines to that system and replace any defective CCAs. The ethernet connection between the safety computer and the control computer is defective. Replace the e-box. The RS-485 connection between the lid lock CCA and the control computer is defective. Check the RS-485 connections and replace the wiring if they are defective. The RS-485 connection between the e-rotor and the control computer is defective. Determine whether any of the e-rotor cables or bucket cables are pinched, smashed, or kinked. Also check them for continuity and shorts. The safety computer, the control computer, the lid lock CCA, or the e-rotor does not have the correct input voltage. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1802': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1802', name: 'System problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'SoftwareCRCFault', occursDuring: 'Self-tests during startup state.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the control computer detects an incorrect CRC with either control, lid lock CCA, or e-rotor software.', possibleCauses: 'The control computer is defective or there is a loose connection. Replace the e-box The control CCA or its connections are defective. Power cycle to clear the alarm. There is a software issue. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card. The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the lid lock CCA for proper operation and connections. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Determine whether any of the e-rotor cables or bucket cables are pinched, smashed, or kinked. Also check them for continuity and shorts. Check the log files to determine which system is at fault. Then check power and communication lines to that system. An e-rotor component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. Replace the e-rotor only when the problem becomes frequent.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1803': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1803', name: 'Data corruption', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'ConfigBackupFileReadFailure', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the backup configuration file in the configuration directory is corrupt or missing.', possibleCauses: 'There is a software issue. Power cycle to clear the alarm. Check configurations in the data system manager. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1804': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1804', name: 'Data corruption', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'ConfigDefaultFileReadFailure', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the template for the configuration file in the software directory is corrupt or missing.', possibleCauses: 'There is a software issue. Power cycle to clear the alarm. The compact flash card is defective. Check the configurations in the data system manager. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. Replace the compact flash card.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1805': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1805', name: 'Data corruption', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'ConfigFileReadFailure', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the main configuration file is corrupt or missing.', possibleCauses: 'There is a software issue. Power cycle to clear the alarm. The compact flash card is defective. Check the configurations in the data system manager. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. Replace the compact flash card.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1807': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1807', name: 'Version mismatch', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'UnsupportedICDInterfaceVersionAlarm', occursDuring: 'When selecting protocol.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the software interface version reported by the device is not supported by the data system manager.', possibleCauses: 'The device software was updated, but the data system manager software was not. Upgrade the data system manager software or downgrade the device software.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1809': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1809', name: 'Invalid device type', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'DeviceInvalidAlarm', occursDuring: 'When selecting protocol.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the device is not configured in the data system manager.', possibleCauses: 'The device is not properly configured in the data system manager. Configure the device in the data system manager.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1811': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1811', name: 'System problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Software', alarmId: 'SoftwareTaskFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when there is a software problem.', possibleCauses: 'The data for the barcode reader is accessed by different software tasks. This creates a queue for this data, and one of the tasks timed out. Power cycle to clear the alarm. If the alarm persists, there may be an issue with either the e-box or the software. Troubleshoot these systems and reload software as needed. There is a software issue. Reboot the device.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1903': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1903', name: 'Centrifuge problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Self test', alarmId: 'SafetyT1CentrifugePowerFault', occursDuring: 'Self-tests during startup state.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when commands from the safety computer fail to power on the centrifuge motor controller or power it off.', possibleCauses: 'The CMC relay is defective or there is a loose connection. Troubleshoot the CMC relay for proper operation and connections. The AC monitor CCA or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the AC monitor CCA for proper operation and connections. The centrifuge motor controller or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the CMC line voltage circuit for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective. Power cycle to clear the alarm.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1904': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1904', name: 'Outer lid lock problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Self test', alarmId: 'SafetyT1LidPowerFault', occursDuring: 'Self-tests during startup state.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when commands from the safety computer fail to power on the lid or power it off.', possibleCauses: 'The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the lid lock power circuit for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective. Power cycle to clear the alarm.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1907': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1907', name: 'Vibration sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Self test', alarmId: 'T1VibrationSensorFault', occursDuring: 'Initial centrifuge ramp up.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the output from the vibration sensor increases by more than 0.1 G.', possibleCauses: 'The vibration sensor is defective or there is a loose connection. Troubleshoot the vibration sensor system for proper operation and connections. The chiller CCA or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the chiller system for proper operation and connections. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '1908': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '1908', name: 'Hydraulic sensor', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Self test', alarmId: 'T1HydraulicsSensorFault', occursDuring: 'Self-tests during startup state.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the hydraulic pressure sensor reports that the hydraulic pressure did not change by at least 0.1 bar during the startup state.', possibleCauses: 'The hydraulic pressure sensor is defective. Compare hydraulic pressure sensor against a calibrated gauge. If defective, replace the pressure sensor. The connection between the hydraulic pressure sensor and the control CCA is defective. Check these components for a poor connection. The +24 V DC supplied to the hydraulic pressure sensor is out of range or has a defective connection. Check system DC voltages.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2000': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2000', name: 'Bucket sensor problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'Bucket1BucketSensorFailureAlarm', occursDuring: 'During protocol line/bucket sensor calibration.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the bucket interface sensor calibration value is out range. This range is configured for each protocol.', possibleCauses: 'The component bag set was loaded incorrectly. Load the buckets correctly. The bucket interface sensor is dirty. Clean the bucket interface sensor and verify it is operating correctly. The bucket interface sensor, the bucket CCA, or the connections are defective. Test the sensor while the centrifuge is spinning. The problem may only show in the g-field. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Determine whether any of the e-rotor cables or bucket cables are pinched, smashed, or kinked. Also check them for continuity and shorts. The RS-485 communication line to the e-rotor has noise or a failure. Troubleshoot what may be causing the noise or failure. The error may resolve on its own.', suggestedActions: ''),
