    '2016': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2016', name: 'Line sensor problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'InitialCalTubingLoadedAlarm', occursDuring: 'Startup', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the line sensor calibration ends with a gain value at 255 or an LED adjust value at 0.', possibleCauses: 'The buckets were loaded during the line sensor calibration. Ensure nothing is loaded in the buckets or line sensor during startup. Do not load the buckets until the proper loading screen appears. The line sensor is dirty. Clean the line sensor and verify it is operating correctly. The line sensor or its connections are defective. Problem may appear only in the g-field. Test the sensor while centrifuge is spinning. The e-rotor or its connections are defective. Determine whether the e-rotor communication/power/data cable and e-rotor to bucket cables are pinched, smashed, or kinked. Also check for continuity and shorts. The RS-485 communication line to the e-rotor has noise or a failure. Troubleshoot what may be causing the noise or failure. The error may resolve on its own.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2100': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2100', name: 'Centrifuge speed too high', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetyCentrifugeOverspeedFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the rotation sensor detects that the centrifuge speed exceeds 3250 rpm.', possibleCauses: 'The rotation sensor is defective. Replace the rotation sensor. The gap between the rotation sensor and the speed ring is less than 1 mm or greater than 1.5 mm. Check the rotation sensor for correct sensor gap, sensor function, and connections. The centrifuge motor controller or its connections are defective. Check the centrifuge motor controller operation and connections. The centrifuge motor or its connections are defective. Check the centrifuge motor operation and connections. The CMC programming or commissioning is defective. Check the centrifuge motor controller programming and commissioning. Power cycle to clear the alarm.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2200': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2200', name: 'System problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetySoftwareCRCFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the safety computer detects an invalid CRC with the safety software.', possibleCauses: 'Safety software is stored on the compact flash card and loaded via the control computer during startup. The safety computer reads the file CRC during startup. This alarm is raised if the CRC is incorrect. Power cycle to clear the alarm. There is a software issue. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card. The control computer or its connections are defective. Check the control computer for proper operation and connections. Replace the e-box if they are defective. The safety computer or its connections are defective. Check the safety computer for proper operation and connections. Replace the e-box if they are defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2201': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2201', name: 'System problem', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetySoftwareWatchdogFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the safety computer detects a software watchdog failure.', possibleCauses: 'The safety computer did not receive the watchdog message back from the control computer. Power cycle to clear the alarm. An e-box component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable. The ethernet connection between the safety computer and the control computer is defective. Check the ethernet connection between the control and safety computers. The control computer or its connections are defective. Check the control computer for proper operation and connections. The safety computer or its connections are defective. Check the safety computer for proper operation and connections. The compact flash card is defective. Replace the compact flash card. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm the system power supply voltages are in range under load.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2202': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2202', name: 'Centrifuge system--Obsolete', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetyCentrifugeCommandFault', occursDuring: 'This alarm is not used.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the safety computer detected that there is power to the centrifuge motor controller, which should be disabled.', possibleCauses: 'The centrifuge motor controller is defective. Replace the centrifuge motor controller. The CMC relay is defective. Replace the CMC relay.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2203': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2203', name: 'Outer lid system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetyLidCommandFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the safety computer detects an invalid lid lock power command from the control computer.', possibleCauses: 'The safety computer received a command from control to energize the lid lock power while the centrifuge is spinning. Check the log files to determine which system is at fault. Then check power and communication lines to that system. Power cycle to clear the alarm. There is a software issue. Reload the software with a known version, such as a released CD from a spares kit, and upload files from the usb drive stored with the device. The control computer or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the control computer to check for proper operation and connections. If it defective, replace the e-box. The safety computer or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the safety computer to check for proper operation and connections. If it defective, replace the e-box. The system power supply voltages are out of range. Confirm system power supply voltages are in range under load. The compact flash card is defective. Replace compact flash card. An e-box component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2300': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2300', name: 'Hydraulic pressure too high', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetyHydraulicOverpressureFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the safety system detects that the hydraulic over-pressure switch opened and removed power to the hydraulic pump motor.', possibleCauses: 'The hydraulic pressure in the system rose above the over-pressure switch\'s set point, which is 3.5 bar. This could be a result of a problem with loading or a problem with blood processing. It could also be a problem with the hydraulic system, such as too much air or an obstruction. Check the loading. If the control system did not trigger an over pressure condition but the over pressure switch opened, the hydraulic pressure sensor or its connections might be defective. Troubleshoot the hydraulic system to determine if there is a problem with the sensor, and check for an air leak or an obstruction. If there was not an over pressure condition of 3.5 bar or greater in the hydraulic system to trigger the over-pressure switch then the over-pressure switch or its connections might be defective, or the set point might be too low. Power cycle to clear the alarm. A hydraulic component may have failed. To determine the occurrence rate of failure, perform a RAT search on the log files; set the search parameters for one month at minimum. Longer is preferable.', suggestedActions: ''),
    '2401': DlogAlarmReference(machine: 'reveos', code: '2401', name: 'Outer lid system', statusLine: '', messageType: '', dlogText: '', category: 'Safety', alarmId: 'SafetyLidStateBadWithCentrifugePoweredFault', occursDuring: 'Always active.', detection: 'This alarm is raised when the safety computer detects that the lid was unlocked while the centrifuge was spinning.', possibleCauses: 'The lid lock CCA or its connections are defective. Check the log files to determine if the safety system or the control system is at fault. Then troubleshoot the lid system (control or safety side) to find the fault. The optical control sensors or their connections are defective. Check the optical control sensors. The e-box or its connections are defective. Troubleshoot the e-box and replace it if it is defective.', suggestedActions: ''),
